      <div type="clause" n="71">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 71</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="71" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="86" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif monnes eage him mon ófaslea oððe his hand oððe his fot, ðær gæð gelic bot to eallum: VI<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_71.lnote.oe.9"/> pæningas ⁊ VI scill. ⁊ LX scill. ⁊ ðriddan dæl<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_71.lnote.oe.10"/> pæninges.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="71" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="86" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif monnes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_71.lnote.oe.1"/> eage him mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_71.lnote.oe.1"/> ofaslea oððe his hond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_71.lnote.oe.1"/> oþþe his fót, ðær geð gelic bot to eallum: VI peningas ⁊ VI scillingas ⁊ LX scll' ⁊ þriddan dæl peniges.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_71.lnote.oe.6"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="71" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="86" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf mon him …<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_71.lnote.oe.3"/> ofsléa oþþe his hand oððe his fótt, ðær gæð gelic bot tó eallu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>: syx penegas ⁊ syx scill' ⁊ syxtig scill' ⁊ ðriddan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_71.lnote.oe.4"/> dæl peniges.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="71" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="87" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis oculum uel manum uel pedem excutiat alicui, parem emendationem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_71.lnote.oe.5"/> componat de singulis, id est LXVI solid. et VI den. et terciam partem unius denarii.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="90" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif monnes eage him mon ófaslea oððe his hand<ptr type="editorNote" n="22" target="#Af_71.attnote.fn.22"/> oððe his fot, ðær gæð gelic bot to eallum: VI pæningas<ptr type="editorNote" n="23" target="#Af_71.attnote.fn.23"/> ⁊ VI scill. ⁊ LX scill. ⁊ ðriddan dæl pæninges<ptr type="editorNote" n="24" target="#Af_71.attnote.fn.24"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="75" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="362" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif monnes eage him mon ófaslea oððe his hand oððe his fot, ðær gæð gelic bot to eallum: VI pæningas ⁊ VI scill ⁊ LX scill ⁊ ðriddan dæl pæninges.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="87" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_71.lnote.de.1"/> man jemandes Auge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_71.lnote.de.2"/> ihm ausschlägt oder seine Hand<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_71.lnote.de.3"/> oder seinen Fuss<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_71.lnote.de.4"/> [abhaut], da tritt gleiche Busse für alle [drei Fälle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_71.lnote.de.5"/>] ein: 6<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_71.lnote.de.6"/> Pfennige und 6 Schill. und 60 Schill. und dritten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_71.lnote.de.7"/> Theil eines Pfennigs.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone knocks out a person’s eye or [cuts off] his hand or his foot, the same compensation applies to all [three cases]: 6 pence and 6 shillings and 60 shillings and a third of a penny.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="91" ed="#attenborough"/>If a man's eye is knocked out, or if his hand or foot is struck off, the same compensation shall follow them all—6 pennies, 66 shillings and the third part of a penny<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_71.attnote.n.1"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="363" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone strikes a man’s eye from him, or his hand or his foot, an equal compensation applies to all: 6 pennies and 6 shillings and 60 shillings and a third of a penny.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>inspired by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_43">Abt 43</ref> <quote>It was Alfred's return to the topic, in making a point that was ... one of Æthelberht's, which argues that the one was inspired by the other (n. 85)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>inspired by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_54">Abt 54–54.5</ref> <quote>It was Alfred's return to the topic, in making a point that was ... one of Æthelberht's, which argues that the one was inspired by the other (n. 85)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>inspired by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_69">Abt 69</ref> <quote>It was Alfred's return to the topic, in making a point that was ... one of Æthelberht's, which argues that the one was inspired by the other (n. 85)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="363"><label>same sum</label> <ref target="clause:Af_47">Af 47</ref> <quote>See n. 168 to §50.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="272"><ref target="clause:Af_6-1">Af 6.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="301"><ref target="clause:Af_6-1">Af 6.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="351"><ref target="clause:Af_47">Af 47</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_71.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">86</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">syx pen. ⁊ syx sc. ⁊ syxtig <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">syx pen. ⁊ syx sc. ⁊ syxtig Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_71.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">86</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dæle pen. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dæle pen. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_71.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">86</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geändert in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_71.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">86</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Rasur vor</hi> ges</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">erasure before ges</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_71.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">87</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">emendam <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">emendam Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_71.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">86</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">him <hi rend="italic">nochmals, ausradirt; folgendes</hi> oþþe <hi rend="italic">unterstrichen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">him repeated, erased; the following oþþe underlined</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_71.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">86</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dr. <hi rend="italic">B</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dr. B</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_71.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Beeinflusst durch Abt 43. 69?</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Influenced by Abt 43. 69?</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_71.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">B cor. streicht das Auge, vielleicht weil schon <hi rend="italic">o.</hi> 47 behandelt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">B cor. deletes the eye, perhaps because it was already dealt with <hi rend="italic">above</hi> 47</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_71.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Gliederbussen 5; Hand 9</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Gliederbussen 5; Hand 9</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_71.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Fuss 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Fuss 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_71.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ebenso and. Germ.; Wilda 761</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Likewise among other Germanic peoples; Wilda 761</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_71.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. o.</hi> Af 47³</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See above</hi> Af 47³</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_71.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Der Akkus., auch in Q Inst., ist nicht zu ‘emendieren’, sondern originales Anakoluth wie <hi rend="italic">o.</hi> 43</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The accus., also in Q Inst., is not to be ‘emended’, but is an original anacoluthon as <hi rend="italic">above</hi> 43</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_71.attnote.fn.22" n="22" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">90</biblScope></bibl><label>hand</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">Gyf mon him…ofsléa oððe his hand</hi>. B. But signs of erasure after <hi rend="italic">him</hi> and <hi rend="italic">oððe</hi> underlined.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_71.attnote.fn.23" n="23" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">90</biblScope></bibl><label>pæningas</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">penegas</hi>. B. <hi rend="italic">peningas</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_71.attnote.fn.24" n="24" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">90</biblScope></bibl><label>pæninges</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">peniges</hi>. B &amp; H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Af_71.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. cap. 47, note.</seg></note>
